{
  "schema": 1,
  "description": "Qualification floors (REVAMP_PLAN §15.1 plus package acceptance floors). Each floor names the scenario (`qual file::test fn`) and the QUAL metric it judges. `wave` is the wave from which scripts/qualify.ps1 enforces it. Release builds only; hardware is recorded with the evidence. `platforms` (optional, WP4.2) lists where a floor is enforced; a floor without it is enforced everywhere. The per-object fsync throughput floors are Windows dev box floors (§15.1): WSL's ext4 disk image runs the bare create/write/fsync/rename loop at about 138 objects/s (`fs_objects_per_s`, measured by WP4.2), below the floor itself, so the Linux subset (scripts/qualify.sh) records them without enforcing them. The qual_wp4_4_seal floors are CCR-WP4.4-4 (registered by WP4.INT); its staging-cost ratio is checked inside the scenario. The wave 5 floors (WP5.INT) are the WP5 acceptance numbers (REVAMP_PLAN §14.5b): CCR-WP5.1-4 (acceptance (c) on event_cost_5k_1k, 10x of WP4.INT's 269 ms; the storm-shaped event_cost_storm_5k_1k tracked on its own), CCR-WP5.2-6 and CCR-WP5.3-4. A floor with `heavy: true` judges a scenario that qualify.ps1/qualify.sh run only with -Heavy/--heavy (the two-hour WP5.1 daemon workloads): it is enforced only when its scenario ran. wp5_2_copy_2000_files_speedup needs TKFS_BASELINE_BIN (the 6298d0b release build).",
